::DATA_Q1_Ontology::What does an ontology primarily define? {
=Concepts and relationships within a domain
~Only passwords used by a system
~Physical network cable lengths
~A list of unrelated files
}

::DATA_Q2_Primary_Key::What is the main purpose of a primary key in a relational table? {
=Uniquely identify each record
~Encrypt every column
~Connect the database to the internet
~Automatically delete duplicate tables
}

::DATA_Q3_Normalization::Why is database normalization used? {
=To reduce unnecessary duplication and update problems
~To place all information in one very large table
~To remove every relationship between tables
~To prevent SQL queries from being executed
}

::DATA_Q4_SQL_Aggregation::Which SQL clause is normally used to create groups before applying functions such as COUNT or AVG? {
=GROUP BY
~ORDER BY
~DELETE
~DROP TABLE
}

::DATA_Q5_Supervised_Learning::What distinguishes supervised machine learning? {
=The model learns from examples containing known labels or target values
~The model never uses training data
~The model works only with database passwords
~The model cannot be evaluated
}

::DATA_Q6_Embeddings::What is the purpose of an embedding in natural language processing? {
=Represent text as numerical vectors that capture semantic information
~Convert every sentence into a database password
~Delete all relationships between words
~Replace model evaluation with manual guessing
}
